# Animations — Framer Motion

Use **`framer-motion`** (`motion` / `AnimatePresence`) for page and UI motion.

## Rules

- Prefer Framer Motion over CSS keyframes / Tailwind `animate-*` for meaningful UI motion
- Animate: route/page transitions, list enter/exit, modals/drawers, feedback (success/error), subtle hover where it helps UX
- Wrap conditional UI with `AnimatePresence` when mounting/unmounting
- Keep motion purposeful and light — no noisy perpetual animation
- Do not animate layout thrashing; prefer `opacity`, `y`, `scale`, and shared layout sparingly
- HeroUI handles its own micro-interactions; Framer Motion covers app-level transitions and custom motion wrappers

## ❌ BAD

```tsx
<div className="animate-bounce">{children}</div>
```

## ✅ GOOD

```tsx
import { motion, AnimatePresence } from 'framer-motion'

<AnimatePresence>
  {open && (
    <motion.div
      initial={{ opacity: 0, y: 8 }}
      animate={{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }}
      exit={{ opacity: 0, y: 8 }}
    >
      {children}
    </motion.div>
  )}
</AnimatePresence>
```
